Ladybird encloses a CSS rectangle by flooring its near edges and
ceiling its far edges in device pixels. Empty dimensions remain
empty. A local background can therefore cover the entire scrollable
area when the container starts at a fractional pixel coordinate.

Blink uses the same edge rounding and empty-dimension handling in
gfx::ToEnclosingRect(). WebKit derives dimensions from floored and
ceiled corners in enclosingIntRect(), with a separate helper for
preserving empty rectangles. Gecko’s BaseRect::RoundOut() likewise
rounds both corners before deriving the size. Ladybird keeps empty
dimensions empty, matching Blink and retaining its clipping behavior.

Form controls retain a shared side length for their square painting
rectangle. Their dimensions are rounded explicitly rather than
derived from an enclosing rectangle, which can grow each axis by a
different amount when their origins have different fractional parts.
